course: dictionary
lesson: 14919
title: Bending light
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To refract means to bend. When light passes from one material into another, such as from air into water, it changes direction a little. «The straw looks bent when you put it in a glass of water.» The straw is not really bent. The light coming from it bends as it leaves the water.
explain: Refraction is the noun for this bending. To check a meaning, swap it into the sentence: if «bend» still makes sense, you have found the right idea. «The swimming pool looks shallower than it is» because light refracts as it reaches your eyes.
explain: Sound and other waves can refract too, when they change speed. Safety first: pools are deeper than they look, so never jump or dive into water when you cannot see the bottom.
fact: Refract means to bend light as it passes from one material into another.
fact: Refract is a verb: refracts, refracted, refracting. The noun is refraction.
fact: Light refracts when it moves from air into water or glass, because it changes speed.
fact: A prism refracts white light and splits it into a rainbow of colours.
fact: Lenses in glasses and magnifying glasses refract light so we can see clearly or see things bigger.
exercise: «The light refracted as it entered the water.» What does refracted mean? | Turned into sound | Stopped dead at the surface | Went out completely | *Bent as it passed into another material
exercise: «The straw looks bent in the glass of water.» Why does it look bent? | *Light refracts as it leaves the water, so the straw looks bent | The straw really is bent | The water makes the straw grow
exercise: What is the noun for refract? | reflection | refracts | *refraction | refracted
test: «The prism refracted white light into a rainbow.» What does a prism do to white light? | *It refracts it, splitting it into a rainbow | It stops it completely | It turns it into sound | It makes it louder
test: Why does a swimming pool look shallower than it is? | *Because light refracts as it reaches your eyes | Because the pool is painted blue | Because the water is cold | Because the bottom is missing
exam: Which sentence uses refract correctly? | I refract my lunch every day | The dog refracts the ball across the park | Refract is the name of a colour | *The lens refracts light, so the letters look bigger
